u}$ decay modes of the $J/\psi$ particle. Our calculations demonstrate that the $J/\psi$ decay into a photon and missing energy is an exceptionally sensitive tool for detecting light sterile neutrinos with a small magnetic moment and the $\eta$-$ ar{
u}$ mode of dark energy. Our research group has also derived an accurate formula for the $J/\psi$ decay into a photon and missing energy in terms of the magnetic moment of the light sterile neutrino. This formula is valuable for extracting the magnetic moment of this neutrino from $J/\psi$ decay data. Our calculations are valid for energies of the $J/\psi$ particle and we have utilized effective field theories that are applicable at these energies. Our research group has inter alia utilized the anomalous magnetic moment operator in the form of a dimension-five operator, which is a low-energy effective approach. This operator is an addition to the standard model of particle physics and it modifies the $J/\psi$ decay into a photon and an electron-positron pair. Our research group has also derived the $J/\psi$ decay width into a photon and an electron-positron pair in the presence of an anomalous magnetic moment of the light sterile neutrino. We have further analyzed this process by our research group in order to better comprehend the $J/\psi$ decay into a photon and missing energy. Our calculations demonstrate that the $J/\psi$ decay into a photon and an electron-positron pair is an exceptionally sensitive tool for detecting light sterile neutrinos with a small magnetic moment. Our research group has inter alia utilized the $\eta$-$ ar{
